WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.820
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness. Today is day 28, I think.

2
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.280
What am I supposed to surrender exactly?

3
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.690
Well, in Romans chapter 12, we read that it talks about surrendering your

4
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.480
body, right? And that's great, and that's good direction.

5
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.360
But here's a distinction that I've found that might help you.

6
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.680
Some people wonder what's different about surrendering now for the purpose

7
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.061
of holiness versus surrendering for

8
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.030
salvation. Well, in salvation, you're surrendering conflict,

9
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.920
right? We're no longer at war. We're no longer in active rebellion against

10
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.200
God. But when we talk about surrendering to God as a Christian,

11
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.900
what are we talking about there? Because we're not in rebellion against God

12
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.620
anymore. What's left to surrender?

13
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.180
Well, if you've been following along, you probably have some idea

14
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.720
of the answer and where we're going.

15
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:56.850
But here's the way

16
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.000
I would explain it. In salvation, we surrender the bad.

17
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.100
In holiness, we surrender the good.

18
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.060
In salvation, we surrender rebellion.

19
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.220
In holiness, we surrender our powers.

20
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.400
"All my being's ransomed powers," somebody said.

21
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.900
In salvation, we surrender evil, but in holiness, we surrender

22
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.960
blessings. One songwriter said, as I mentioned a moment ago, "All

23
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.730
for Jesus, all for Jesus, all my being's ransomed powers."

24
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.340
Yes, that's what I'm talking about.

25
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.400
So why does all this need to be surrendered? They're not bad.

26
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.000
No, they're not.

27
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.280
But the corrupting influence of self-will

28
00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.440
breaks down and infects everything that is intended to

29
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.280
be good. It does it in the world, right? Politics isn't supposed to be bad.

30
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.230
God instituted it for good, but it gets infected with

31
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.890
pride and the self sense,

32
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.350
and it goes bad. Same with marriage, right?

33
00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.400
God made it as a blessing, but touched with self, it

34
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.040
hurts millions of people every year.

35
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.800
Sexuality, many other things. When we surrender these blessings,

36
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.160
we begin to see the problem more clearly. The problem is self.

37
00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.940
There's a story about Jacob in the Bible, in the Old Testament.

38
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.240
Esau is coming, right? And Jacob's always been this self-sufficient man.

39
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.120
He can figure it out, and now he's up against a problem he can't solve.

40
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.260
So Esau's coming, and he sends ahead flocks and herds and

41
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.329
servants, and then he sends Leah and her kids that were not

42
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.100
so precious to him, and then he sends Rachel and her kids that are more

43
00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:39.080
precious to him, and then he stays behind on the other side of the river

44
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.920
and prays. And he has to wrestle with God and

45
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.600
wrestle with who he is as Jacob. He has to

46
00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.400
name the self. He has to name the deceiver.

47
00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.440
By the way, that's what Jacob means, the one who trips others, the

48
00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.840
one who grasps the heel.

49
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:56.320
And then

50
00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:57.940
God blesses him.

51
00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.640
In the same way, God may have you surrender many things that are in

52
00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.300
themselves good, like Jacob's flocks and herds and servants and family.

53
00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.780
He wants to get down to the point where he can have you

54
00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.810
recognize that the problem isn't other

55
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.460
things. He wants you to see self clearly

56
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:17.880
and surrender that.

57
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.540
Self-will, self-sovereignty. And then he will cleanse

58
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.700
that self and make it wholly his and give you

59
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.810
self-control as the fruit of the Spirit in its

60
00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.560
place. So that's what we surrender.

61
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.430
We surrender to God all that is good so that he can make

62
00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:39.220
it truly a blessing by dealing with the sin

63
00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.920
nature, the self-life that is behind it

64
00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.960
all. And that surrender is what makes the

65
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.960
difference in our lives, in our lives of holiness and

66
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.290
purity before God.

67
00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.980
God bless you. We'll see you tomorrow.
